<title>POLAND: Mostostal-E to get subsidiary dividend.</title>
<headline>Mostostal-E to get subsidiary dividend.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction and trading firm Mostostal Export SA will receive a dividend from its 69-percent controlled subsidiary  Bankowe Towarzystwo Leasingowe SA (BTL), Mostostal said in a statement on Friday.</p>
<p>Mostostal said BTL had decided at its general shareholders meeting that it would earmark its 1995 and 1996 net profit totalling 30.2 million zlotys for dividend. @</p>
<p>It said BTL also voted in favour of a capital increase through a rights issue after which Mostostal-Export's holdings would fall to 43 percent while another shareholder Bank Przemyslowo-Handlowy (BPH) would boost its stake to 57 percent from the present 25 percent.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
